  "summary": "On 7 June 1494 Ferdinand II of Aragon, Isabella I of Castile and John II of Portugal set a line of demarcation running from pole to pole, 370 leagues west of the Cape Verde islands. It placed the eastern end of Brazil in the Portuguese zone; the line was approximate, and later disputes over the Spice Islands and the River Plate followed.",
